      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't address either concern. You're not a prescriber, and the dose would be 5,100 mg/day, about double the maximum. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere's what can move this forward:\n- **The prescriber confirms or corrects the order.** The prescriber who owns the order can talk to the pharmacist. If they really intend a dose this far above the maximum, that needs a documented clinical rationale and pharmacist review. It shouldn't be entered through me on a non-clinician's say-so.\n- **A corrected, in-range order.** If the intended dose was something like 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily, tell me and I'll enter it. Please have the prescriber confirm it first.\n\nI can also help with a non-clinical task, such as drafting a message to the prescriber or pharmacy about the dose question."
      }
